preConditionHook:
// EL: avgUpperTail = average((high - maxlist(open, close)) / (high - low +
// epsilon), windowBars), and the mirror over the lower tail for the short
// side. The window is INCLUSIVE of the current bar.
//
// Average recomputes from scratch every bar (EL_Summation_Probe, 2,808/2,808)
// and the averaged quantity is a price EXPRESSION with real history -- not an
// EL variable -- so this is a fresh loop over price, NOT the
// WFSafe_AvgTrueRange rolling accumulator and NOT the zero-filled variable
// mirror BarRangeAboveStd needs. Summed newest-first, EL's Summation order.
//
// The epsilon is the corpus's zero-range guard (the literal CloseRangePosition
// carries): EasyLanguage raises a RUNTIME divide-by-zero error on a zero
// denominator, so it is added inside the ratio rather than branched around,
// and it is an input so the ratio's low bits match the twin's.
//
// maxlist/minlist select among open and close -- tick-grid price operands,
// the scope their ACCEPTED row allows -- so plain comparisons stand in.
avgUpperTail = 0.0;
avgLowerTail = 0.0;
for (int i = 0; i < (int)windowBars; ++i) {
    bodyTop = open[i];
    if (close[i] > bodyTop) bodyTop = close[i];
    bodyBottom = open[i];
    if (close[i] < bodyBottom) bodyBottom = close[i];
    avgUpperTail += (high[i] - bodyTop) / (high[i] - low[i] + epsilon);
    avgLowerTail += (bodyBottom - low[i]) / (high[i] - low[i] + epsilon);
}
avgUpperTail /= (int)windowBars;
avgLowerTail /= (int)windowBars;
